'\\}\n\\end{align*}", "MATH_0001": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/V) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/h_V^\\#$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0003": "$j_{V!}\\mathcal{G} \\to j_{V!}(*) = h_V^\\#$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0005": "$j_!\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$j_{U!}(j_!\\mathcal{G}) \\to j_{U!}(*) = h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0007": "$j_{U!}j_! = j_{V!}$", "MATH_0008": "$j^{-1}$", "MATH_0009": "$j_!$", "MATH_0010": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{H} \\to h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/h_U^\\#$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{H}_\\varphi$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n(a : W \\to U)\n\\longmapsto\n\\{ s \\in \\mathcal{H}(W) \\mid \\varphi(s) = a\\}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0016": "$j^{-1}\\mathcal{H}_\\varphi$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{C}/V$", "MATH_0018": "$$\n(a : W \\to V)\n\\longmapsto\n\\{ s \\in \\mathcal{H}(W) \\mid \\varphi(s) = f \\circ a\\}\n$$", "MATH_0019": "$j^{-1} = j_{U/V}^{-1}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{H}_\\varphi$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{C}/V$", "MATH_0022": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{H}' = \\mathcal{H} \\times_{\\varphi, h_U^\\#, f} h_V^\\#\n\\ar[rr]^-{\\varphi'} & & h_V^\\#\n}\n$$", "MATH_0023": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/h_V^\\#$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{H}'_{\\varphi'}$", "MATH_0025": "$j^{-1}\\mathcal{H}_\\varphi$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-relocalize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-essential-image-j-shriek}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fe18cdd322bd8c3d11eed4a624d35d26f4b9bcb27617eb56618a2270939edad7", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:9b5623fa319a557a543612a9df6cc26a14cd97c28d9832a1f9913faaadd38667", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b876c0378d3ba6da6abe5eec186d88bd2ee8560e09205b38f5f05b770af1bbc0", "source_text": "Proof of (2). Recall that the identification\n<MATH_0001>\nsends <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>\nand similarly for\n<MATH_0004>.\nThus <MATH_0005> is mapped to\n<MATH_0006>\nand (2) follows because <MATH_0007>\nby Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nThe reader can now prove (1) by using that <MATH_0008> is the\nright adjoint to <MATH_0009> and using that the rule in (1)\nis the right adjoint to the rule in (2). Here is a direct proof.\nSuppose that <MATH_0010> is an object of\n<MATH_0011>. By the proof of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthis corresponds to the sheaf\n<MATH_0012> on <MATH_0013> defined by the rule\n<MATH_0014>\non <MATH_0015>. The pullback <MATH_0016> to\n<MATH_0017> is given by the rule\n<MATH_0018>\nby the description of <MATH_0019> as the restriction\nof <MATH_0020> to <MATH_0021>.\nOn the other hand, applying the rule to the object\n<MATH_0022>\nof <MATH_0023>\nwe get <MATH_0024>\ngiven by\n<MATHSEG_0001> and <MATHSEG_0002>\nwhich is exactly the same rule as the one describing\n<MATH_0025> above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6fea66801e9a3769efa262894afe2a839fa9f85ea4bdc1668804975a766c2555", "unit_id": "tag:04IL:proof"}
